CAT = "hcapLaw"; SEG = "LAW"
Q = [
("Which provision of the Wildlife Act 1976 is the basis of the annual deer hunting licence?",
 "Section 29", ["Section 28", "Section 36", "Section 42"],
 "Section 29 allows the Minister to grant a licence to hunt and kill exempted wild mammals with firearms. NPWS issues the deer hunting licence under it."),
("A deer hunting licence normally runs from:",
 "1 August to 31 July", ["1 January to 31 December", "1 April to 31 March", "1 November to 31 October"],
 "Licences are annual. A section 29 licence ends on the next 31 July."),
("To hunt deer with a rifle in the open season you need:",
 "A firearm certificate and a licence", ["A firearm certificate and a landowner's note", "A deer hunting licence alone", "A landowner's written note alone"],
 "The Firearms Acts control the rifle and the Wildlife Acts control the hunting. You must hold both."),
("A farmer who owns the land and wants to shoot deer on it with a rifle:",
 "Still needs a deer hunting licence", ["Needs no licence on his own land", "Needs only a firearm certificate", "Needs only a note from a neighbour"],
 "Section 28 requires a licence under the Act as well as being a qualified person for the land. Owning sporting rights satisfies only the second."),
("You may hunt deer with firearms only on land where you:",
 "Hold sporting rights or authority", ["Have driven past without objection", "Have a friend within a mile", "Know the local Coillte forester"],
 "Section 28 limits firearm hunting to a qualified person: someone with sporting rights, or a guest, agent or holder of written authority from the person who has them."),
("The licence declaration states that your rifle meets the minimum requirements of:",
 "S.I. 239 of 1977", ["S.I. 307 of 2009", "The Control of Dogs Act", "The Game Act 1925"],
 "The Wildlife Act 1976 (Firearms and Ammunition) Regulations 1977 set the type of firearm and ammunition that may be used on deer. S.I. 307 of 2009 covers secure storage."),
("Under the 1977 Regulations, which rifles may be used on deer?",
 "Centre-fire rifles of set calibre and energy", ["Any bolt-action rifle with a scope", "Rimfire rifles with soft-point bullets", "Any rifle fitted with a sound moderator"],
 "The Schedule allows only centre-fire rifles meeting a minimum calibre, muzzle energy and bullet weight. Other types and calibres must not be used."),
("Using a shotgun to kill deer is:",
 "An offence", ["Allowed with slugs", "Allowed on Coillte land", "Allowed in the male season"],
 "Section 33 makes it an offence to kill or injure a protected wild animal, other than a hare, with a shotgun, unless it is done under a licence from the Minister. Deer are protected wild animals."),
("Shooting at deer from a car that is parked is:",
 "An offence under the Wildlife Act", ["Lawful once the engine is switched off", "Lawful on a quiet forest road", "Lawful with a deer licence"],
 "Section 36 bars hunting any wild animal by means of a mechanically propelled vehicle, whether the vehicle is moving or stationary."),
("Deer may be hunted only between:",
 "One hour before sunrise and one hour after sunset", ["Sunset and sunrise", "Midnight and 6 a.m.", "Sunrise and sunset, with no allowance either side"],
 "Section 37 bars hunting protected animals from one hour after sunset to one hour before sunrise. Coillte can restrict hours further on its land."),
("Using a lamp or torch to hunt deer is:",
 "An offence unless licensed", ["Allowed on private land", "Allowed if the lamp is red", "Allowed in the female season"],
 "Section 38 prohibits artificial light, mirrors and dazzling devices in hunting. Lamping for deer needs a licence, for example for research."),
("Which of these is an offence when killing any wild mammal?",
 "Using tracer shot", ["Using a high seat", "Using binoculars", "Using a bipod"],
 "Section 33 makes it an offence to kill or injure any wild bird or wild mammal with a spring gun or with tracer shot."),
("Which of these is prohibited for hunting deer?",
 "Snares and similar devices", ["A stalking high seat", "A hand-held stalking stick with a tip", "A pair of binoculars and a rangefinder"],
 "Section 34 bars hunting any wild bird or mammal with a trap, snare, net, line, hook, arrow, dart or spear, or with poisoned or stupefying bait."),
("Deer may be controlled outside the open season to stop damage under:",
 "A Section 42 permission", ["A notice to the Gardai", "Any hunt club's rules", "A Coillte tender document"],
 "Section 42 lets the Minister give permission, or authorise a person, to capture or kill protected animals causing serious damage to crops, woodland and other property."),
("Who can apply for a Section 42 permission for deer damage?",
 "The owner or occupier", ["Any deer hunting licence holder", "The local hunt secretary", "A Garda superintendent"],
 "Section 42 permission is sought by the owner or occupier of the property suffering the damage, or a person they authorise, and is valid only for the period stated."),
("A Section 42 permission requires you to:",
 "Report the deer killed as directed", ["Keep every deer shot for sale", "Ignore the open season dates", "Hunt only by lamp at night"],
 "A permission is valid only for the stated period and the holder must furnish details of animals taken at the times and in the form the permission specifies."),
("Live wild deer are legally owned by:",
 "No one until lawfully taken", ["The owner of the nearest land", "The State at all times of year", "The licence holder for the area"],
 "Wild deer are ferae naturae, without an owner, until reduced into possession. The lawful hunter then owns the carcase."),
("Red deer may NOT be hunted in:",
 "County Kerry", ["County Wicklow", "County Donegal", "County Meath"],
 "The Open Seasons Order excludes the county of Kerry for red deer, protecting the native Killarney herd."),
("A deer hunting licence allows you to hunt:",
 "Only within the open season", ["At any time of the year", "Only on weekends and holidays", "Only with hounds or dogs"],
 "NPWS requires all wild deer open season dates to be followed. Hunting outside the season needs a separate Section 42 permission."),
("Are open seasons the same for male and female deer?",
 "No, they are set separately", ["Yes, they are always the same", "Only the male season is set", "No, each hunter picks dates"],
 "The Open Seasons Order lists male deer and female and antlerless deer separately for each species."),
("Deer open seasons are set by:",
 "A ministerial order", ["The Deer Alliance board", "The board of Coillte", "The Garda Commissioner"],
 "Open seasons come from an order made by the Minister under section 25 of the Wildlife Act, as later amended."),
("A deer hunting licence holder is expected to:",
 "Make an annual return of deer shot", ["Hand your rifle to the Gardai each spring", "Hunt only in groups of three", "Pay a fee on every deer shot"],
 "NPWS expects a return of deer shot, and section 29 lets the Minister require the species and numbers shot."),
("A standard firearm certificate application goes to:",
 "A Garda superintendent", ["The nearest NPWS office", "The county council", "Coillte"],
 "Applications for a firearm certificate other than a restricted one are made to the superintendent of the district where the applicant lives."),
("A firearm certificate limits:",
 "The firearm and ammunition held", ["Only the hours you may shoot", "Only the land you may shoot on", "Only the age of the holder"],
 "It authorises the named person to possess, use and carry the specified firearm and to hold no more than the amount of ammunition specified."),
("A deer rifle applicant must name land where:",
 "Deer are likely, with permission", ["A gun club already shoots", "Hunting is banned in law", "No dwelling is within five miles"],
 "The Garda guidelines require named land with the likelihood of the right deer species and an invitation, booking or authority from the owner or occupier."),
("Land named for a rifle is checked by Gardaí for:",
 "Stops, roads, rights of way, dwellings", ["Only the size and shape of the land area", "Only the soil type and drainage", "Only the tree species planted"],
 "Land is not intrinsically safe or unsafe. Gardaí look at rights of way, public roads and footpaths, nearby dwellings, suitable stops and topography."),
("The minimum age to hold a firearm certificate is:",
 "16", ["14", "18", "21"],
 "Under the Firearms Act a person under 16 is disentitled. Training certificates can allow supervised use by younger people."),
("Which person is disentitled from holding a firearm certificate?",
 "A person of intemperate habits", ["A person who rents rather than owns a home", "A person over sixty", "A first-time applicant"],
 "The Firearms Act disentitles people under 16 and those of intemperate habits, among others, from holding a certificate."),
("A sound moderator fitted to a deer rifle is, in law:",
 "A firearm needing authorisation", ["A harmless accessory", "A scope accessory", "Banned in all cases"],
 "The Firearms Acts define silencers as firearms. Those used only on long rifled firearms are not restricted but still need a Garda authorisation under the 1990 Act."),
("A Coillte sporting licence allows the licensee and nominated stalkers to hunt deer:",
 "Only in the open season", ["All year in the forest", "Only during the rut", "Without a deer hunting licence"],
 "A Coillte licence does not override the Open Seasons Order. Out-of-season shooting needs a separate Section 42 permission."),
("Deer hunting licences are now applied for through:",
 "The online Heritage Licensing Portal", ["Any Garda station", "A county council office", "Coillte's forest office"],
 "NPWS issues the section 29 deer hunting licence online through the Heritage Licensing Portal, where the applicant also declares compliance with S.I. 239 of 1977 and uploads firearm certificate details."),
("Killing any deer with a rifle in the closed season is lawful only:",
 "Under ministerial permission", ["On your own registered land", "At first light only", "With a Coillte deer tag"],
 "Outside the open season deer may be killed only under a ministerial permission such as Section 42, or an equivalent licence."),
]
